ENGLISH VERSION (courtesy translation; the French text prevails)
======================================================================

PhoenOS is free software whose source code anyone may read, modify and
redistribute, under a few simple conditions that protect users: knowing what
they install, who it comes from, and whether it was modified.

1. DEFINITIONS
 - "Software": PhoenOS, its source code, programs, build tools,
   documentation and images, in any version published by the Original
   Publisher.
 - "Original Version": a version published by the Original Publisher
   (e.g. "PhoenOS 0.7.1").
 - "Modified Version": any software derived from the Software whose code,
   programs, configuration or content were changed, added or removed, even
   partially.
 - "PhoenOS Identity": the name "PhoenOS", the logo, the boot banner and the
   official images of the Software.
 - "Third-Party Driver or Extension": a driver, library (.psl), program or
   application (.poe) written by someone other than the Original Publisher
   that works with PhoenOS through its public interfaces (system calls, file
   formats, driver interface).

2. GRANT
You may, worldwide, free of charge, for an unlimited time, use the Software
for any purpose (personal, educational, professional), study it, copy it,
modify it and redistribute it, subject to the conditions below.

3. REDISTRIBUTION CONDITIONS (original or modified)
 a) Same license: any redistribution is under this license, whose full text
    must be included.
 b) Free of charge: the Software and its Modified Versions are redistributed
    free of charge. You may not charge for the right to receive or use them.
    (You may charge for a separate service: installation, support, training,
    hardware.)
 c) Notices kept: you keep the copyright notices and this license.

4. ADDITIONAL CONDITIONS FOR A MODIFIED VERSION
 a) Name: a Modified Version is named "PhoenOS <nickname>", where <nickname>
    is chosen by its author (e.g. "PhoenOS Aurora"). It may not be called
    "PhoenOS" alone, nor claim or imply that it is the official version.
 b) Explicit notice of modification: the Modified Version states clearly and
    visibly (a MODIFICATIONS file at the root, the project's front page, and
    the system's boot screen or message):
      - that it is modified;
      - the Original Version it derives from (e.g. "PhoenOS 0.7.1");
      - the original publisher (Anatole, PhoenOS);
      - the publisher of the Modified Version (name or pseudonym and link).
 c) PhoenOS Identity unmodified: the PhoenOS image (logo, banner, official
    images) is reproduced as is whenever shown; it is not altered, replaced,
    or used to present your own logo as PhoenOS's. You may add your own
    identity beside it, provided it cannot be confused with ours.

5. THIRD-PARTY DRIVERS AND EXTENSIONS
 a) A Third-Party Driver or Extension that includes no code of the Software
    is not a Modified Version: its author publishes it under the license of
    their choice and need not use the name "PhoenOS <nickname>".
 b) The name "PhoenOS" may not designate a third-party driver or extension as
    if it were official. Only drivers published by the Original Publisher are
    "official PhoenOS drivers".
 c) Third-party drivers and extensions are used AT THE USER'S OWN RISK: a
    driver runs with broad access to hardware and may malfunction, lose data
    or damage it. The Original Publisher does not review them and is not
    responsible for them.

6. CONTRIBUTIONS
Unless agreed otherwise in writing, any contribution (code, patch,
documentation) you voluntarily send to the Original Publisher is placed under
this license and may be included in the Software, including in future
Original Versions. You warrant that you have the right to provide it.

7. NO WARRANTY; LIABILITY
The Software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or
implied (quality, fitness for a purpose, absence of defects). An operating
system under development may contain errors that lose data or damage
hardware: back up your data and test in a virtual machine. To the extent
permitted by law, the Original Publisher and contributors are not liable for
damages arising from use of the Software.

8. TERMINATION
If you violate this license, your rights end. They are reinstated if you cure
the violation within 30 days of being notified (first violation). People who
received the Software from you keep their rights as long as they comply.

9. GOVERNING LAW
This license is governed by French law, without prejudice to mandatory rules
that apply where a consumer lives.
